Clip cheat names to the row they are drawn in.

Cheat names come from the community usrcheat.dat, not from a designer, and some
are whole sentences: "Unlimited Use of Konami Code for Full Power-up with 30
Lives" is a real Contra 4 entry. menu_render_cheats drew the name unclipped at
the left of the row and the < ON/OFF > control right-aligned in the same row, so
a long name ran straight through the control and off the panel.

Adds draw_string_fit(), a width-limited draw that ellipsizes on a codepoint
boundary - the database is full of non-ASCII names and cutting mid-sequence
draws a replacement box rather than a shorter name - and gives the name only
the room left beside the value. cp_w() is factored out of str_w() so both
measure the same way.

Candidate for tenlevels' tree - not yet submitted. Drop this patch once it
lands upstream rather than carrying it forever.

